 recent cold history and fever (37.5°C) suggest this, but LAP elevation and persistent constitutional symptoms make it lower likelihood", "Myeloproliferative Neoplasm (other than CML): elevated LAP supports this, though specific subtype determination requires further testing"], "alarm_features": ["Unintentional weight loss", "Fever (37.5°C)", "Significant leukocytosis with normal differential"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Myeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.26694179640729176, "posterior": 0.26334043925535155, "danger": 0.9, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["Elevated LAP moderately supports myeloid neoplasms with increased blasts (B1) and moderately excludes CML within chronic myeloproliferative neoplasms (B3)."], "evidence_against": ["Absence of blasts weakly excludes myeloid neoplasms (B1) and weakly supports chronic/reactive processes."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B1.1", "B1.2", "B1.3"], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.5, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.8, "interrupt_relevance": 0.9, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": ["acute myeloid leukemia", "myelodysplastic syndrome with excess blasts", "chronic myeloid leukemia in blast crisis"]}, "B3": {"id": "B3", "label": "Chronic Myeloproliferative Neoplasm (chronic/accelerated phase)", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.1, "danger": 0.6, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Elevated LAP and lack of blasts in the differential strongly argues against chronic-phase myeloproliferative neoplasms (B3) and CML blast crisis, while the abs…"]}, "B5": {"id": "B5", "label": "Reactive / Non-malignant Leukocytosis", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.206, "danger": 0.3, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Elevated LAP and lack of blasts in the differential strongly argues against chronic-phase myeloproliferative neoplasms (B3) and CML blast crisis, while the abs…"]}, "B1.1": {"id": "B1.1", "label": "De Novo Acute Myeloid Leukemia (AML)", "parent": "B1", "level": 2, "status": "live", "prior": 0.2080065946030845, "posterior": 0.16808964207788396, "danger": 0.9, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": ["Constitutional symptoms provide weak support for de novo AML (B1.1) but do not override the elevated LAP which is more characteristic of MDS-EB. The absence of…"], "evidence_against": ["Elevated LAP and lack of blasts in the differential strongly argues against chronic-phase myeloproliferative neoplasms (B3) and CML blast crisis, while the abs…"], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.5, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.6, "interrupt_relevance": 0.9, "level_role": "disease_class", "classification_axis": "etiology", "representative_diseases": []}, "B1.2": {"id": "B1.2", "label": "CML Blast Crisis", "level": 2, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.07, "danger": 0.8, "parent": "B1", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Elevated LAP contradicts chronic-phase myeloproliferative neoplasms and CML blast crisis but supports MDS-EB and reactive leukocytosis."]}, "B1.3": {"id": "B1.3", "label": "Myelodysplastic Syndrome with Excess Blasts (MDS-EB)", "level": 2, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.025, "danger": 0.7, "parent": "B1", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Absence of blasts strongly excludes CML blast crisis and weakly excludes AML and MDS-EB, while weakly supporting chronic-phase myeloproliferative disorders."]}}, "frontier": ["B1.1", "B1.1"], "other_mass": 0.0, "actions_taken": [{"t": 3, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the subacute presentation with constitutional symptoms argue against MDS-EB in favor of more chronic myeloproliferative disorders?", "summary": "Subacute presentation provides neutral evidence for MDS-EB and chronic-phase myeloproliferative neoplasms but weakly excludes reactive leukocytosis."}, {"t": 3, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the elevated leukocyte alkaline phosphatase (LAP) contradict chronic myeloproliferative neoplasm as the diagnosis?", "summary": "Elevated LAP contradicts chronic-phase myeloproliferative neoplasms and CML blast crisis but supports MDS-EB and reactive leukocytosis."}, {"t": 4, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the presence of constitutional symptoms (unintentional weight loss and fever) support de novo AML (B1.1) as a high-priority myeloid neoplasm despite the elevated LAP?", "summary": "Constitutional symptoms provide weak support for de novo AML (B1.1) but do not override the elevated LAP which is more characteristic of MDS-EB. The absence of blasts remains a critical exclusion factor for AML."}, {"t": 4, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the elevated LAP and absence of blasts in the peripheral differential argue against de novo AML (B1.1) in favor of CML blast crisis or chronic-phase myeloproliferative neoplasm (B3)?", "summary": "Elevated LAP and lack of blasts in the differential strongly argues against chronic-phase myeloproliferative neoplasms (B3) and CML blast crisis, while the absence of blasts weakly excludes AML (B1.1) but does not eliminate it entirely."}, {"t": 5, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the presence of constitutional symptoms (unintentional weight loss and fever) support de novo AML (B1.1) despite the elevated LAP?", "summary": ""}, {"t": 5, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the absence of blasts in the peripheral differential and elevated LAP strongly contradict de novo AML (B1.1) in favor of reactive leukocytosis (B5) or chronic myeloproliferative neoplasms (B3)?", "summary": ""}], "deliberation": {}, "interrupt": {"active": false, "reason": "No universal instability markers (airway, respiratory, circulatory, neurological, or haemorrhagic) are present. No time-critical syndrome patterns (e.g., STEMI, stroke, septic shock) are indicated by the current presentation.", "required_actions": []}, "termination": {"ready_to_stop": false, "termination_type": "continue", "reason": "Leading terminal branch (B1.1) posterior (0.168) < 0.75 AND dangerous parent branch (B1, danger=0.9, posterior=0.263) remains unresolved. Critical discriminators (e.g., bone marrow biopsy, LAP quantification) are untried but necessary to distinguish myeloid neoplasms from reactive processes."}, "turn_budget_used": 4, "estimated_remaining_value": 1.3, "max_turn_budget": 5, "latest_action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "diagnosis_readiness_score": 0.20560766856903515, "benchmark_output_ready": false, "static_question": "Which of the following is the most likely diagnosis?", "static_options": [{"id": "A", "description": "Acute lymphoblastic lymphoma"}, {"id": "B", "description": "Chronic lymphocytic leukemia"}, {"id": "C", "description": "Chronic myeloid leukemia"}, {"id": "D", "description": "Leukemoid reaction"}, {"id": "E", "description": "Multiple myeloma"}], "seen_evidence_ids": [], "seen_evidence_phenotypes": "{'Elevated leukocyte alkaline phosphatase', 'constitutional symptom', 'Myeloid leukemia', 'fatigue', 'Absent leukocyte alkaline phosphatase', 'Leukocytosis', 'weight loss'}", "mode_policy": {"benchmark_purity": true, "allow_external_knowledge": true}, "answer_option_mapping": {}, "root_revision_needed": false, "max_tree_depth": 3, "reasoning_ledger": {"anchor": {"hypothesis": "B1", "t": 0, "posterior_at_anchor": 0.438}, "leader": {"branch_id": "B5", "label": "Reactive / Non-malignant Leukocytosis", "posterior": 0.206, "leading_since_t": 0, "n_revisions": 0}, "leader_evidence": {"confirming": 5, "disconfirming": 4, "last_disconfirming_digest": "Elevated LAP and lack of blasts in the differential strongly argues against chronic-phase myeloproliferative neoplasms …"}, "action_intents": [{"t": 3, "in